      "stageRecord": "The embedded verb raises from the previously established V position to the adjacent head-final I, leaving a silent head trace. This analysis adopts V-to-I adjunction for Japanese finite predicates; it does not treat the surface past form as an unanalyzed V terminal. A relative C projection is then constructed, and the silent object operator moves from its established complement position to Spec-CP, leaving an NP trace. The operator binds that trace under c-command, and the trace remains locally governed by the verbal projection containing the verb's head chain. The operator movement is entirely within the embedded clause. The resulting CP denotes a predicate of the missing object, not a clause in which 本 itself has raised. Both the relative C and the operator are unpronounced.",
