      "stageRecord": "The relative CP is adjoined to N′ on the left of the nominal projection headed by 本, giving the externally headed interpretation ‘the book that Hanako read.’ The nominal head is identified with the variable bound by the relative operator; it is not another occurrence in the operator's movement chain. The resulting NP combines with accusative を to form the matrix object KP. This object is first placed in the complement position of 買う, following the underlying matrix subject 太郎が. Matrix past I is introduced above VP and licenses the subject's nominative Case. The completed embedded verb–tense complex now receives the collective realization 読んだ. The three supplied tokens 読, ん, and だ are orthographic portions of that inflected predicate, not three independently selected syntactic words. The lexical dictionary form and abstract tense remain in the tree, with their realization recorded collectively.",
